Consider the following x86/NASM code or specification:
```nasm
// C++ code (Slide 6.23):
int a = 5;
int b = 3;
int c = a + b;

; NASM equivalent:
mov eax, 5
mov ebx, 3
add eax, ebx
```
In the C++ to NASM translation example on Slide 6.23 (`ch06_hopngu_phan1.pdf`), what are the values of `EAX` and `EBX` after `add eax, ebx`, and in what order do the tools `Compiler`, `Assembler`, and `Linker` process a C/C++ source file (`.c/.cpp`) into a final executable (`.exe/ELF`)?
